# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production overrides. Vite loads `.env` first, then `.env.production` on top
# of it for `npm run build`, so everything not named here (VITE_EXT_APP_ID,
# VITE_EXT_APP_PASSWORD) still comes from `.env`.
#
# SAME-ORIGIN BUILD. Both values are deliberately EMPTY: axios falls back to
# relative URLs, so the SPA calls `/login`, `/ext-api/wow-attendance/*` and
# `/uploads/wow_attendance/*` on whatever host serves the page.
#
# Why empty rather than a hostname:
#   - No CORS. The service ships `Cors::permissive()`, which we do not want
#     facing a public network; same-origin removes the need for it entirely.
#   - No rebuild when the domain changes. VITE_* values are inlined at BUILD
#     time, so a hardcoded origin can only be corrected by rebuilding.
#   - `/login` stays correct. DEPLOYMENT.md keeps POST /login on duerp-api
#     while attendance lives on :8083; the frontend posts /login to this same
#     origin, so only a shared host serves both.
#
# REQUIRES the nginx config in duerp-face-recognition-backend/docs/DEPLOYMENT.md
# on the host serving this bundle: `/ext-api/wow-attendance/` and
# `/uploads/wow_attendance/` proxy to 127.0.0.1:8083, everything else to
# duerp-api on :8080. Serve the SPA from anywhere else and every call 404s.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_ATTENDANCE_END_POINT=
VITE_ATTENDANCE_UPLOADS_ORIGIN=
